From: dArkOS RG52 Mini port
Subject: The screens swap on the Back key, not on L3

The core swapped the top and bottom screens when L3 was pressed (Toggle, by
default: each press). On the RG52 Mini L3 is the switch under the left stick
(BTN_THUMBL, a GPIO key), which a hard push of the stick closes by accident
(seen on the device: L3 down for 0.7 and 3 s in a row while playing): the
screens changed places in the middle of a game, and the small bottom screen
filled the panel.

They now swap on each press of the Back key (KEY_FN in the device tree,
BTN_TRIGGER_HAPPY1 from the pad; nothing else uses it, and the RetroPad has
no button for it, so the core reads its state from the pad's event device with
EVIOCGKEY, which takes no events from RetroArch). The "Screen Swap Mode"
option (toggle or hold the button) is gone. Which screen is the prominent one
is still chosen in the core options (Prominent 3DS Screen). L3 is still the
3DS's HOME button.

